        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "A good secondary lecturer for the later parts of the class with informative slides and thorough coverage of physiology. While there weren't lecture recordings, he did post his full slideshow to the course page ahead of the lecture. His tests were completely based on the lectures, were fair, and required only notes review to succeed. A funny guy.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "He's so sweet, and you can tell that he genuinely cares about his students and what he teaches. The material was challenging for sure and at times I struggled to understand his lectures, but I feel that in the end I learned a lot from him. The exams are not easy and you definitely need to study and take notes, but he's a great professor!",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Amazing Professor! One of my favorite classes. You definitely have to show up to lecture or you won't know what is going on but he is very engaging and you can tell he loves what he is teaching. Exams are difficult but as long as you prep well you will do well. Honestly cannot talk highly enough about this professor.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Professor Bement is definitely one of my favorite professors. You can tell he knows what he is doing and makes the course very enjoyable. He has a good sense of humor, which he mixes in with class a lot. All the notes are written on the board and there's no power point, but if you keep track of the notes and review you'll be fine.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Bill is a really nice guy.  He can be a little squirrely at times and likes to swear.  Exams suck, there are a ton of things to remember but if you study your notes a lot you'll do fine.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "funny guy, trys to keep you entertained. teaches in a very organized clear format",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 4
            }
